# .gitignore — files Git must never track in the QuickBites backend.
#
# This file lists generated or machine-local artefacts that should stay out of
# version control: Python bytecode caches (__pycache__, *.pyc), pytest's cache
# directory, virtual environments (.venv, venv), packaging output such as
# *.egg-info, build and dist directories, and local environment files (.env)
# that may hold database URLs or other secrets. Keeping these out of the
# repository avoids noisy diffs, prevents leaking credentials, and keeps every
# developer's checkout reproducible from pyproject.toml alone. It contains no
# functions; each non-comment line is a glob pattern evaluated by Git relative
# to the repository root, and new tooling artefacts should be appended here.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.env
